Package: ggutils
Title: Utilities for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.0.2
Authors@R:
    person("Zhang Jun", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "junjun@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: A collection of utility functions for 'ggplot2'. It currently
    provides 'guide_axis_smart()', a smart axis guide for discrete axes with
    many categories: it selects which labels to show, arranges them
    overlap-free over several rows or columns, and connects each label to
    its tick with a leader line. The package is meant to grow with further
    'ggplot2' helpers. The overlap-free one-dimensional arrangement is a
    port of the 'smartAlign' algorithm from the 'circlize' package and of
    the box arrangement from the 'ComplexHeatmap' package.
